    {
      "text": "No man can serve two masters, Matt. 6:24 (Luke 16:13; 3 Ne. 13:24). served God with fastings and prayers, Luke 2:37. worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve, Luke 4:8. Lo, these many years do I serve thee, Luke 15:29. he that is chief, as he that doth serve, Luke 22:26. If any man serve me, let him follow me, John 12:26. not reason that we should … serve tables, Acts 6:2. Serving the Lord with all humility, Acts 20:19. angel of God, whose I am, and whom I serve, Acts 27:23. henceforth we should not serve sin, Rom. 6:6. we should serve in newness of spirit, Rom. 7:6. by love serve one another, Gal. 5:13. receive the reward of the inheritance: for ye serve the Lord, Col. 3:24. from dead works to serve the living God, Heb. 9:14. have grace, whereby we may serve God acceptably, Heb. 12:28. serve him day and night in his temple, Rev. 7:15. his servants shall serve him, Rev. 22:3.",
